[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
so it reads as one bug with one fix queued. Read by tenant, by booking form and by what the reporters
actually describe, it holds more than one problem. Each has a different fix, and each now has its own
ticket; the table counts them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October: the parser is fixed, and the hint won't be fixed because booking-v3 is retired.
The one-day shift was in neither. Its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

Counted the way the desk counts: by the cause the tenant gives each report, with duplicate rows from the
overlapping export counted once. The one-day moves stay counted where they are filed and get their own row
and ticket.

## After #4471 closed

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: `parser` fixed by "fix(dates): parse dd/mm for
eu locales", and `hint` won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired. The parser and hint tickets are
closed with those reasons. Neither outcome touches `shift`: a date that moves by one day is not read month first, and
it does not come through the booking-v3 form. That ticket stays open until someone fixes it.

## `parser` · the shared parser reads day-first dates month first

Every tenant on file writes the day first (asked of the platform in `locales.ts`, not typed in a list).
The shared parser reads every date month first, so a day-first date comes out with day and month
swapped: "Booked for 2 March. The invite says 3 February." This covers reports from the app, from email,
and from the booking-v2 form. Fix: parse with the tenant's locale. Fixed when #4471 closed: "fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales".

## `hint` · booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY under its date field

Day-first tenants who run booking-v3 show their people a month-first hint. People type what the hint
says, and the form reads it the tenant's way, so the date flips before the parser sees it. Only reports
that came in through the form, from booking-v3 tenants, are this problem. The parser fix does not touch
it. Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, so its hint reaches no one and no new reports of this kind
can come in.

## `shift` · the date moves by one day

The desk already marked these in its notes as "read as a one-day move". They stay counted under `parser`,
where their tenant files them, but a footnote is not a ticket. They are not a swap. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May."
"Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting." The day changes with where
the invite is read, which points at a date sent as midnight and shown in another time zone. Neither the
parser fix nor retiring booking-v3 reaches it. Still open.

## Read the cause from the tenant, not the intake tag

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser the moment it arrives. The "intake tagged" column above
shows how often that guess disagrees with the tenant's locale and form. Count by tenant.

## Why one ticket hid several

Decision 0001 merges on the subject line alone, and reporters describe every problem here with the same
words: "wrong day", "date is wrong". Same subject, different causes. The decision stays as accepted; a
new record should replace it with a rule that keys on cause (tenant, form, channel), as
[the triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already computes.

